From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mykhailo Klimnyk <109966003+mykhailoklimnyk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_qca_8021q: survive a port leaving its bridge

qca_8021q_xmit() takes the bridge of a frame with offload_fwd_mark from
dp->bridge and hands it to br_vlan_enabled() unchecked. A frame the
bridge queued can reach the tagger after dsa_port_bridge_destroy() has
cleared dp->bridge, and br_vlan_enabled(NULL) then oopses in softirq:

  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 00000000000009d0
  pc : br_vlan_enabled+0x0/0xc
  lr : qca_8021q_xmit+0x54/0x1d0
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception in interrupt

Seen on a Redmi AX5400 (QCA8337 under qca-8021q) at "ifdown -a" with
traffic towards a LAN port, about one time in three.

Read dp->bridge once, drop a bridge-forwarded frame whose port is no
longer in a bridge, and let the readers finish before the bridge is
freed.

Signed-off-by: Mykhailo Klimnyk <109966003+mykhailoklimnyk@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/net/dsa/port.c
+++ b/net/dsa/port.c
@@ -471,6 +471,10 @@ static void dsa_port_bridge_destroy(stru
 	if (bridge->num)
 		dsa_bridge_num_put(br, bridge->num);
 
+	/* A tagger's xmit may still hold the pointer it read from dp->bridge;
+	 * it runs under rcu_read_lock_bh().
+	 */
+	synchronize_net();
 	kfree(bridge);
 }
 
--- a/net/dsa/tag_qca_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_qca_8021q.c
@@ -63,24 +63,32 @@ static struct sk_buff *qca_8021q_xmit(st
 				      struct net_device *netdev)
 {
 	struct dsa_port *dp = dsa_user_to_port(netdev);
+	/* dsa_port_bridge_destroy() clears dp->bridge while frames are still
+	 * on their way here, so look at it once.
+	 */
+	const struct dsa_bridge *bridge = READ_ONCE(dp->bridge);
 	u16 queue_mapping = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
 	u16 tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_standalone_vid(dp);
 	u8 pcp;
 
 	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
-		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
+		/* The bridge queued the frame and the port left the bridge
+		 * before it got here. The bridge's VLAN no longer includes
+		 * the port; dsa_user_xmit() frees what we do not return.
+		 */
+		if (unlikely(!bridge))
+			return NULL;
 
 		/* A VLAN-aware bridge carries its own VID; the switch
 		 * forwards on that one.
 		 */
-		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
+		if (br_vlan_enabled(bridge->dev))
 			return skb;
 
-		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
-	} else if (dp->bridge && dp->bridge->tx_fwd_offload &&
+		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge->num);
+	} else if (bridge && bridge->tx_fwd_offload &&
 		   is_unicast_ether_addr(eth_hdr(skb)->h_dest)) {
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
+		struct net_device *br = bridge->dev;
 		u16 pvid;
 
 		/* A unicast frame sent on a bridged port itself, not by the
@@ -92,7 +100,7 @@ static struct sk_buff *qca_8021q_xmit(st
 		 * (imprecise RX). Broadcast and multicast keep the port's VLAN.
 		 */
 		if (!br_vlan_enabled(br))
-			tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp));
+			tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge->num);
 		else if (skb_vlan_tag_present(skb) ||
 			 skb->protocol == htons(ETH_P_8021Q))
 			return skb;
